{"id": "EUVD-2026-48929", "enisaUuid": "38b47af2-253c-3c42-a4cb-839c80113744", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix double-free in SMB2_ioctl() replay\n\nA response-bearing attempt can return a replayable error and free its\nresponse buffer. If SMB2_ioctl_init() fails before the next send, cleanup\nretains the previous buffer type and frees that response again.\n\nReset response bookkeeping before each attempt to prevent the stale free.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:50:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:26", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0be4bc64882edaefaaee8d1e27d083643eb778e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96fcfc8ae7359346156e492ca610e830d2649ad6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/276c8efbc49f9303ac76d0d4deab7128581b0f3b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc65ffb4ef1bf540da16b17c225ae51091e07d72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9bbadb6c94583e3b4af1afc449bfceb1d1ddec9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-w5jf-frgq-phfp", "CVE-2026-64385"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "225d1e5b-f270-3170-8d62-1762bf6c88b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "2d15ffb1-43d7-37eb-aeb0-f70e2f7afb82", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.39"}, {"id": "36672676-f3f9-391c-a9d1-5e35844c76f4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <fc65ffb4ef1bf540da16b17c225ae51091e07d72"}, {"id": "3bec5465-b813-353b-8f1d-49ab004835ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "72a22267-391c-3a1f-934c-97bc4bde7b6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <9